# Keep shell scripts LF even on Windows checkouts (autocrlf): bash rejects CRLF
# (`set -euo pipefail\r` -> "invalid option name"). Applies to build_native.sh,
# the verify-*.sh helpers, and any AppRun/entrypoint scripts.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts are Windows-native; keep them CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# CI fixture projects: LF on every host, because their line endings are part
# of a hash. `pyproject_sha256` in a committed pylock.*.toml is taken over the
# file's bytes, so with autocrlf a Windows checkout would produce CRLF, change
# the digest, and make `kivyforge lock --check` fail there while passing on the
# ubuntu runner. A gate whose result depends on which host ran it is not a gate
# (the rule test-matrix.md and pyrightconfig.json both already enforce).
tests/fixtures/apps/** text eol=lf
